## OT-T3: text tier, not the meaning rule
OT-T3 text strengths (first search): fair, then 9 weak. Its term weights (UD-019): decide df 5657 (idf 5.25), the absent word df 0 (14.59), supplier df 34 (10.36), contract df 91149 (2.39). A chunk holding decide + supplier + contract has 0.55 of the weight -> fair. Only one of its key words is absent; "supplier" is rare but present (34 chunks).

## R-9 trigger
Constraint 1 (every verified off-topic question ends only-weak) cannot be met on the default model by any k, Ls, Lf, because OT-T3 has a fair text match. Per R-9 the implementation stops and returns a Design Impact; no constraint is relaxed. Without OT-T3, k >= 100 meets constraints 1 and 2 (margins +/-0.0046 to +/-0.0057); constraint 3 (gates) holds by construction (strength does not rank).
